  "hypotheses": [
    "A component can fail closed on malformed, PREPARED, expired, wrong-nonce, structurally rolled-back, cross-inventory, or incorrectly signed HostSnapshot rollback-anchor bytes without treating them as product authority.",
    "A COMMITTED anchor must bind the exact verified inventory coordinates, one-hop signed predecessor-digest linkage, structural monotonic CAS state, configured path, verifier nonce, schema bytes, root quorum, and freshness interval.",
    "The complete verified binding must enter CurrentAuthorityVector and the guarded-read evidence horizon so an older capability authorization is rejected when the caller presents an after-vector with an advanced anchor, freshness receipt, or binding.",
    "The query-trace verifier must observe the same six anchor-vector fields and reject a component/reference observation unless it is explicitly non-product-authorized.",
    "The guarded authorization and operation-admission serialization must retain the exact HostSnapshot anchor binding digest/boundary together with all other component premises, a closed blocker set, and productAuthorized=false."
  ],
