  "limitations": [
    "The anchor, freshness bytes, expected path, verifier nonce, trusted time, and trust context are supplied by the caller. The component does not independently generate the nonce or fetch directly from an external authority.",
    "Structural CAS verification cannot prove authority-side linearization, external monotonic persistence, power-loss durability, reservation recovery, or a real HostSnapshot publisher transaction.",
    "The executable tests use a test root and test keys; they do not prove a production pinned root, HSM/KMS, rotation, revocation, custody, or nonce transport.",
    "CurrentAuthorityVector, the guarded read, and query trace are portable/local components, not mapped target-Qman repository, adapter, controller, or side-effect code.",
    "The carried authority disposition and operation-admission binding are permanently productAuthorized=false. They prevent component-premise laundering but do not prove a SERIALIZABLE product read, committed lease, successful CAS, or pre-side-effect journal fence.",
    "The SQLite reference placeholder is explicitly non-authoritative and is not evidence of an external HostSnapshot rollback authority.",
    "Raw PCI structure and FLR replay now have a separate component-only E2 record; this anchor slice still does not provide a product raw-config collector/provider, target-Qman wiring, complete reset/domain semantics, or a product capability publisher.",
    "There is no target-code mapping, E3 end-to-end product execution, E4 physical qualification, or signed CaseCompletionRecord.",
